WEBVTT

00:00.330 --> 00:02.001
Why did they react that way?

00:02.410 --> 00:04.234
Why do I keep putting this off?

00:04.617 --> 00:09.425
Understanding people explores questions like these across friendships, family life,

00:09.719 --> 00:12.091
learning, work and community life.

00:13.122 --> 00:16.642
Start by separating what happened from your explanation.

00:17.051 --> 00:18.722
A friend has not replied.

00:19.130 --> 00:21.605
That is different from knowing they do not care.

00:21.987 --> 00:26.681
Learn what observations and research can tell you, and what remains uncertain.

00:27.705 --> 00:31.876
Explore motivation, beliefs, emotions and habits.

00:32.285 --> 00:37.004
Ask how circumstances, culture and power affect what someone can do.

00:37.413 --> 00:40.703
Wanting to join an activity does not make transport or

00:40.716 --> 00:42.821
caring responsibilities disappear.

00:43.190 --> 00:45.422
Include yourself in these questions.

00:46.455 --> 00:50.715
Practise asking useful questions and checking that you understood the answer.

00:51.099 --> 00:56.252
Explore truth and lies, including why confidence or body language cannot settle

00:56.265 --> 00:57.490
whether a claim is true.

00:58.538 --> 01:02.429
Then consider cooperation, motivation and boundaries.

01:02.799 --> 01:05.860
Choose a useful next step and review what happens.

01:06.269 --> 01:10.300
Where there is harm or fear, support and safety come before finding

01:10.312 --> 01:11.715
the perfect explanation.

01:12.747 --> 01:14.877
Watch or read each explanation.

01:15.273 --> 01:20.248
Recall the main question, try one fresh situation, then use it during the week.

01:20.617 --> 01:23.436
Deeper exercises and notes are optional.

01:23.845 --> 01:27.123
The conclusion brings the lessons together when you finish.

01:28.163 --> 01:30.880
Bring one situation you want to understand.

01:31.277 --> 01:34.746
Start with Chapter One: Why we misinterpret people.
